<title>USA: US to sell $28.5 bln 2-, 5-yr notes May 28, 29.</title>
<headline>US to sell $28.5 bln 2-, 5-yr notes May 28, 29.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury Department said on Wednesday that it will sell $16.5 billion of 2-year notes on May 28 and $12 bln of 5-yr notes on May 29 to refund $28.858 billion of securities maturing May 31 and to pay down about $350 million.</p>
<p>The notes will be issued on June 2. The two-year notes mature on May 31, 1999, and the five-year notes mature on May 31, 2002.</p>
<p>The CUSIP number for the 2-year notes will be 9128272V3 and for the five-year notes will be 9128272W1.</p>
</text>
